  "title": "The project directory kept growing",
  "summary": "February brought more community-built ways to use Pollinations, broader model choices, and a text API better suited to interactive clients.\n\nCommunity additions ranged from text adventures and image generators to chat apps, bots, a model comparison tool, and Musify. pollinations.diy also joined the monorepo as a browser-based coding assistant.\n\nThe text API added Gemini 2.0 Flash and Flash Thinking, Hormoz 8B, and an o1-mini reasoning option. Image generation gained a turbo option, while OpenAI text requests gained a larger message limit.\n\nFunction calling and provider-backed streaming let clients handle tools and responses as they arrive. Follow-up work improved SSE formatting, cached-stream replay, Cloudflare compatibility, and routing through a shared gateway client.\n\nText requests gained a `private=true` option, and `/openai` requests became private by default. Image prompts gained LlamaGuard checks, with maturity metadata improved for feed listeners.",
